  "rules": [
    "Every SPELL_EFFECT creates a new repeating1s timer and sets the same target integer key7 to7. No buff/alive test in BOOMA01.",
    "Each callback decrements the shared integer before dealing5% current max life. It checks exact zero after damage; other timers are not cancelled.",
    "Death elseif: killer fire, Skeleton King, h0PC(empty), nonzero key7, bone dragon, n004, Tauren. Nonzero includes negative.",
    "Explosion selects enemies of killer owner within450, but damage150 is sourced by the dead bomb target, with chaos/universal. No alive/Avul filter in Destruction01.",
    "One shared dummy owner is killer; each target gets thunderbolt then faeriefire command. RemoveUnit at1sec and timedLife2sec both recorded.",
    "A0IR native armor DataA1 is absent and targs1=none; separate prototype Attack20 registration needs further investigation."
  ],
  "boundaries": [
    "Aslo command execution currently instant. h0JP castpt0.3/castbsw0.51 exist, but full native cast sequencing and missing DataA movement slow are not synthesized.",
    "Web manual target cast available. Unit auto field_ and no A0IP-specific automated slow entry found; no tooltip-based random-target AI invented.",
    "Dummy casts have missing native damage/mana/cooldown/target/cast fields and shared command cancellation. Only requests retained; no automatic area stun/armor reduction asserted.",
    "Null killer GetOwningPlayer(null) semantics unverified; death branch selected and explicit boundary recorded, no fallback to bomber owner.",
    "Real RemoveUnit handle behavior unresolved; jobs stop with a boundary on explicit removed handles, not ordinary death/corpse cleanup.",
    "Host enumeration omits hidden/locust and follows entity insertion order. Timer family is interleaved chronologically, cross-family native ordering remains partial.",
    "Negative shared counters can leave a timer running indefinitely in source. Preserved, not silently capped; normal wave reset still follows host lifecycle.",
    "UnitDamageTargetBJ uses host attack-flag adapter as in existing Bandit/Malfurion branches. Native engine event classification not independently exercised."
  ]
